{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q28209286","formula":"C₂₅H₂₆O₂","hill":"C25H26O2","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":25.0,"H":26.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Diethylstilbestrol monobenzyl ether"},"descriptions":{"en":"Diethylstilbestrol monobenzyl ether (brand names Monozol, Hypantin, Pituitrope), also known as benzelstilbestrol, is a synthetic, nonsteroidal estrogen of the stilbestrol group and an ether of diethylstilbestrol (DES) that is described as a pituitary gland inhibitor (antigonadotropin) and was formerly marketed but is now no longer available. It was first synthesized by Wallace & Tiernan Company in 1952, and was described by them as having only weak estrogenic activity. The drug was used to treat gynecological conditions and infertility in women."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":3036244,"mass":358.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC/C(=C(/CC)\\C1=CC=C(C=C1)OCC2=CC=CC=C2)/C3=CC=C(C=C3)O","inchikey":"FVLDPSZNPFWQQP-OCOZRVBESA-N","iupac":"4-[(E)-4-(4-phenylmethoxyphenyl)hex-3-en-3-yl]phenol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3036244","atoms":53,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.611,"y":-0.114,"z":0.534,"el":"O"},{"x":-8.351,"y":-0.001,"z":-0.136,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.963,"y":-0.6,"z":0.197,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.777,"y":0.485,"z":0.202,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.453,"y":-2.034,"z":0.154,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.293,"y":1.915,"z":0.351,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.489,"y":-0.472,"z":0.286,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.251,"y":0.357,"z":0.113,"el":"C"},{"x":0.109,"y":-0.472,"z":1.531,"el":"C"},{"x":0.245,"y":-0.357,"z":-0.878,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.608,"y":-2.55,"z":-1.271,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.98,"y":2.562,"z":-0.992,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.985,"y":0.242,"z":1.277,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.849,"y":0.356,"z":-1.132,"el":"C"},{"x":2.258,"y":-0.233,"z":0.452,"el":"C"},{"x":1.496,"y":-0.35,"z":1.615,"el":"C"},{"x":1.632,"y":-0.236,